WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.728
Alex asks for a birthday dinner at Juniper House. Type the enquiry

00:00:04.728 --> 00:00:09.456
at the main desk. FormBridge gathers five booking details for staff to

00:00:09.456 --> 00:00:09.850
review.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:15.850
Alex changes the plans by voice: six guests, sometime after eight. Review

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:21.200
the transcript before adding it. The exact time still needs an answer.

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:25.939
Ask the desk assistant for a warm reply suggesting eight-thirty. Read its

00:00:25.939 --> 00:00:30.028
draft, use it in the staff composer, then add the message. Staff

00:00:30.028 --> 00:00:31.050
stays in control.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:36.692
Alex accepts eight-thirty. The time becomes ready, with the staff offer and

00:00:36.692 --> 00:00:41.684
guest acceptance linked as its sources. The earlier correction stays in the

00:00:41.684 --> 00:00:42.100
conversation.

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:47.764
Review the birthday, quiet table and peanut allergy against the guest’s words.

00:00:47.764 --> 00:00:52.779
Keep the requests, approve the brief and save the enquiry. Approval does

00:00:52.779 --> 00:00:54.450
not reserve a table.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:59.744
Open Service planner. The dinner appears at eight-thirty with six guests. Check

00:00:59.744 --> 00:01:04.389
the follow-up for the next shift, then find the saved conversation in

00:01:04.389 --> 00:01:05.550
the enquiry book.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:11.913
Guests can ask questions through the restaurant assistant. Here, it answers the

00:01:11.913 --> 00:01:17.150
kitchen-closing question using Juniper House’s approved information and shows the source.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:22.880
From the first message to the next shift. Open FormBridge and bring

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:24.150
your own enquiry.
